Z||000000||Philphine||11-20-2001||09:32 AM||||<BR>long title but i was trying to be as clear as possible. this kind of branches from artherd's wheel thread.<P>dose an '88 have more room for a higher pos. offset (more backspace) wheel? and, if you try to do the '88 cradle to pre '88 fiero mod will you get that extra room also or somewhere bettween the two? there's no way i could pull off the things he's doing but if the cradle change gave just a bit more room it might be all i need and i could work in that direction.<P>also, if i ever get the 6000 swap done (need it to get a 4.5"/115mm bolt pattern) and then decide to try to switch cradles, would those parts fit on an '88 cradle?<P>what i'm thinking is, i try the brake swap on my '84 cradle. if the wheels i want to try won't fit (did all the measuring i could and it's so close i can't tell without just trying it), but it's just a fraction of an inch then maybe the '88 cradle swap could come into play if the parts will transfer over.<P>did any of that make sence?<P><BR>  <P>------------------<BR>Phil T.<P>start where you are,<BR>use what you have,<BR>do what you can.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||11-20-2001||10:58 AM||||Let me try.<BR>I believe the earlier struts are more "upright" than the 88s. The only way you can swap an 88 cradle into an earlier car is with Held's adapters, and coil-overs.<BR>The coil overs, by themselves, might provide you enough room. <BR>I'm pretty sure the 6000 stuff won't work on an 88. (If you find out different, please let me know.) The knuckles (spindles) are different. Attach differently to the control arms/locating links.<BR>Try giving Dave Held a call. I listened to him talking about coil-overs and such at Ed Parks' swap meet. I think he can answer your questions.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||LZeitgeist||11-20-2001||11:14 AM||||How about installing an '87 V6 onto an '88 4-cyl cradle? Anybody done this? Are the '88 cradles both the same, or do we need to find an '88 V6 cradle?||||reg||1
Z||000003||pherder||11-20-2001||12:34 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by LZeitgeist:<BR><B>How about installing an '87 V6 onto an '88 4-cyl cradle? Anybody done this? Are the '88 cradles both the same, or do we need to find an '88 V6 cradle?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The 88 manual cradles (both 4 and 6) and the V6 automatic cradles are the same.  I believe I had to carve off the center bracket off an 88 4 cylinder automatic cradle to make it the same as the rest.<P>BTW, you need an 88 front engine mount to bolt an earlier V6 engine into the 88 cradle.  <P>Paul||||reg||1
Z||000004||LZeitgeist||11-20-2001||01:27 PM||||Perfect - you're awesome, pherder... THANKS!||||reg||1
